  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Centre of the circle <math><mi>C</mi></math> lies on <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &amp; <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Center of <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Radius of <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/536baa6c-ecf3-4f80-8ab1-a0efa2aebfa1.png\" style=\"width:2.41389in;height:0.99375in\" /><br />Equation of <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
